Loom: gfx11 vector memory ops encode the non-temporal cache policies as GLC / SLC / DLC.

The gfx11 cache-policy row accepted only "regular", so a non_temporal hint was dropped. It now takes
non_temporal, non_temporal_regular and regular_non_temporal for plain loads and stores: the near caches (L0 / L1 / L2)
take the hint as SLC (L2 stream) plus GLC on stores (L0 / L1 miss-evict), the outer one (MALL) as DLC (no
allocation); non_temporal is both, like LLVM's gfx11 nontemporal. Atomics keep their own coherence bits.

Decode's DeltaNet stores its recurrent state with regular_non_temporal (DLC): a write-back copy in the MALL was
flushed during the next SwiGLU GEMV's weight stream (+18 us in each DeltaNet layer's GEMV). Kernels without a cache
hint are unchanged (every other decode / prefill HAL byte-identical).
